INT. GRAND HOTEL - BALLROOM KITCHEN - NIGHT

Stainless steel, white tile, a long pass-through window to the ballroom. Music and applause leak in. Rows of champagne flutes wait on silver trays.

VERA LINDQUIST (40s, black evening gown, a hairpin in her chignon) leans on a counter, calm, arranging canapés on a tray. ISADORA FENWICK (30s, catering uniform, name tag) wipes down the other side of the counter, humming. COLONEL HADDAD (60s, dress uniform, medals, a flushed face) stands in the doorway with a glass. CATERER KIP (20s, apron, clipboard) hovers by the walk-in cooler.

HADDAD
Ladies. I was told there'd be champagne.

VERA
The champagne is in the ballroom, Colonel.

HADDAD
Yes, but this is where the interesting people are.

ISADORA
(smiling)
That's very kind.

HADDAD
Is it?

He drifts closer. Kip glances at his clipboard, then at the door. Vera continues arranging canapés, unhurried.

VERA
Isadora, would you hand me the tongs?

ISADORA
Of course, Vera.

She slides the tongs across. Their fingers brush. A beat too long.

HADDAD
You two know each other?

VERA
We're colleagues.

HADDAD
In catering?

ISADORA
In logistics.

Haddad laughs, tips back his glass. Kip stiffens at the word.

KIP
Ms. Fenwick, the delivery is waiting at the dock.

ISADORA
Thank you, Kip. Tell them five minutes.

Kip nods and slips out. The swinging door sighs shut. Haddad watches it close.

HADDAD
Strange boy.

VERA
He's new.

HADDAD
(low)
Is the car ready?

VERA
Yes.

HADDAD
Then I believe I'll take my champagne.

He holds out his empty glass. Isadora fills it from a bottle on the counter. Haddad drinks, and smiles, and sways a little.

HADDAD (CONT'D)
That's... that's a strange taste.

VERA
It's a very old vintage.

HADDAD
Vera, I don't...

His knees buckle. Isadora catches his arm and guides him smoothly onto a flour sack. Vera pulls the hairpin from her chignon, glances at the ballroom window, and slides it back in.

ISADORA
Four minutes before it takes him.

VERA
Then we have three to be gone.

The door swings open. Kip reappears, white as paper.

KIP
Ms. Lindquist. The Colonel's driver is at the dock.

VERA
Of course he is.

She smooths her gown, takes Isadora's hand, and the two women walk out through the cold-room door as the applause swells.
